WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.576
The iPod nano

00:00:01.388 --> 00:00:02.649
5G freed to

00:00:02.461 --> 00:00:03.569
boot Rockbox

00:00:04.086 --> 00:00:05.489
Viktor Krapivin built

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.574
a fully untethered

00:00:06.386 --> 00:00:07.246
boot chain for

00:00:07.058 --> 00:00:08.366
the iPod nano

00:00:08.178 --> 00:00:09.015
5G

00:00:09.154 --> 00:00:10.415
It loads Rockbox

00:00:10.227 --> 00:00:11.028
straight from the

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:11.960
player's flash

00:00:12.031 --> 00:00:13.316
with no computer

00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:14.366
or button sequence

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:15.486
after installation

00:00:16.006 --> 00:00:17.303
Earlier tricks needed

00:00:17.114 --> 00:00:18.223
a computer every

00:00:18.034 --> 00:00:18.588
boot

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:20.790
He adapted ipod_sun

00:00:21.003 --> 00:00:22.359
a font-based exploit

00:00:22.194 --> 00:00:24.033
that CUB3D first

00:00:23.869 --> 00:00:24.505
showed on the

00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.944
nano 6G and

00:00:25.756 --> 00:00:26.604
7G

00:00:26.805 --> 00:00:27.583
which pairs a

00:00:27.395 --> 00:00:28.609
resource-validation

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:29.517
bypass with a

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:30.555
font-parser bug

00:00:31.094 --> 00:00:32.002
The result is

00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:32.544
a cold

00:00:32.603 --> 00:00:33.782
battery-powered boot

00:00:33.594 --> 00:00:34.643
into Rockbox

00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:35.643
He also made

00:00:35.454 --> 00:00:36.751
the exploit untethered

00:00:36.563 --> 00:00:37.258
on the nano

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:37.977
7G

00:00:38.096 --> 00:00:39.051
and likely the

00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:40.041
6G too

00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:41.580
Full story on

00:00:41.391 --> 00:00:42.287
the dashboard
